        "h": "Three special editions for the 40th anniversary of <em>It</em>",
        "p": "Stephen King's site lists three anniversary editions of <em>It</em>: a US Scribner edition of 1,168 pages with no date announced, a UK Hodder edition of 1,088 pages listed for September 3, and a UK Hodder deluxe limited to 1,010 numbered copies, shipping November 26. The deluxe is not sold in the US or Canada.",
        "src": "StephenKing.com",
        "url": "https://stephenking.com/news"
      },
      {
        "h": "Lividian announces the Robert McCammon Library",
        "p": "Lividian Publications will reissue Robert McCammon's backlist as hardcovers: Smyth-sewn, cloth-bound, with reversible jackets, art by François Vaillancourt and essays by Mathias Clasen. <em>Baal</em> and <em>Bethany's Sin</em> lead in 2026, at four titles a year. <em>The Night Boat</em>, <em>They Thirst</em>, <em>Mystery Walk</em> and <em>Usher's Passing</em> are in production for 2027.",
        "src": "RobertMcCammon.com",
        "url": "https://www.robertmccammon.com/2026/04/17/lividian-publications-announces-the-robert-mccammon-library/"
      },
      {
        "h": "<em>Pan's Labyrinth</em> returns in 3D",
        "p": "<em>Pan's Labyrinth</em> is back in theaters in 3D for its twentieth anniversary: a limited run began October 8 and it went nationwide October 9, from Cineverse and Fathom. It is the film's first 3D release, with a new 4K/HDR master; Aaron Parry of SDFX Studios oversaw the conversion.",
        "src": "Rue Morgue",
        "url": "https://rue-morgue.com/pans-labyrinth-returns-to-theatres-nationwide-in-3d-for-its-20th-anniversary"
      },
